# Normalise line endings.
#
# The shell script matters most: git on Windows with core.autocrlf=true checks
# out LF files as CRLF, and a CRLF shebang makes Linux try to execute the
# interpreter "/bin/sh\r", which does not exist. The container then dies with
# "exec format error" or "no such file or directory" — pointing at /bin/sh,
# which obviously does exist, so the message sends you looking in the wrong
# place entirely.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# Model weights and tokenizer data are binary; never let git touch their bytes.
*.safetensors binary
*.bin binary
*.pt binary
*.pth binary
*.onnx binary
